    {
      "index": 0,
      "sectionIndex": 0,
      "section": "7 days of wear",
      "text": "7 days. That's the new wear clock for Tandem's tubeless Mobi insulin pump, just cleared by the FDA.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 190,
      "endMs": 7560
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "sectionIndex": 1,
      "section": "Doubled vs Omnipod",
      "text": "Omnipod 5, the incumbent tubeless pump, wears 3 days. Tandem has doubled that on the infusion set.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 7560,
      "endMs": 14840
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "sectionIndex": 2,
      "section": "The catch",
      "text": "The catch? The cartridge still changes every 3 days. And the US launch waits until the first half of 2027.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 14840,
      "endMs": 22280
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "sectionIndex": 3,
      "section": "Pharmacy-only",
      "text": "It goes to market pharmacy-only. That reroutes distribution away from the durable equipment channel, which changes the reimbursement path, and the scale mechanics, for a pump launch.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 22280,
      "endMs": 32450
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "sectionIndex": 4,
      "section": "The open question",
      "text": "One wear interval doubled. One distribution channel reset. Whether Tandem takes pump share from Insulet, or just forces Insulet to move, is the open question.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 32450,
      "endMs": 42800
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "sectionIndex": 5,
      "section": "Subscribe",
      "text": "That read, and the deals behind it, in this week's Catalyst Brief. Subscribe free, signal over noise.",
      "cue": null,
      "startMs": 42800,
      "endMs": 49280
    }
  ],
